## Definitions

- **"Copyright Holder"** means Mike Beaumier.
- **"Software"** means everything in this repository or its hosted instances **authored by the Copyright Holder**, including but not limited to: the website and its source code (HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and service worker); the tab editor, lead-sheet renderer, chord and notation tools, and all other application features; parsers, importers, build scripts, data-processing pipelines, and backend code (including database migrations and serverless functions); tests, documentation, schemas, designs, and visual assets; the Copyright Holder's selection, organization, tagging, and metadata for the collection as a whole; and any songs, arrangements, transcriptions, tablature, or other musical content **explicitly authored by the Copyright Holder**. The Software does not include User Content or Third-Party Software.
- **"User Content"** means songs, lyrics, chords, chord charts, lead sheets, tablature, notation (including ChordPro, ABC, and TablEdit files), arrangements, recordings, and similar material that was **not explicitly authored by the Copyright Holder**. This includes material that users submit, upload, import, or contribute through the website, GitHub issues, pull requests, or any other channel, and material taken from third-party sources. User Content found inside data files (such as `.pro` files, `work.yaml` files, or generated indexes) is still User Content.
- **"Third-Party Software"** means code or assets written by others and included in this repository under their own licenses (for example, vendored libraries).
- **"Official Website"** means the instance of the Software hosted by the Copyright Holder, currently at bluegrassbook.com.

